curriculum:
Structure — 192 credit points, including 186 credit points of core subjects (including Chemistry subjects) plus 6 credit points of elective subjects; students need a minimum 70 WAM across the first two years to continue into the third and fourth years;
Chemistry subjects, Wollongong campus (65% or more in NSW HSC Chemistry or equivalent) — Chemistry IA: Introductory Physical and General Chemistry (CHEM101); Chemistry 1B: Structure and Reactivity of Molecules for Life (CHEM102)
Chemistry subjects, Wollongong campus (all other students) and Liverpool campus (all students) — Foundation Chemistry: Properties of Matter (CHEM104); Foundation Chemistry: Reactions and Structures (CHEM105)
Elective subjects (6 credit points) — Sport and Exercise Nutrition (MEDI214); SMAH Research Project (SMAH340); Foundations in Medical Imaging for Healthcare Professionals (SMAH350); Regional Anatomy (MEDI314); SMAH Research Internship (SMAH241)
Work placement and accreditation — The program requires workplace experience or clinical placements in a range of health-related settings; graduates are highly recommended to apply for accreditation with ESSA within 2 years of completing the degree (international students should check the ESSA English language requirements);
